<%# Empty state inside a table body.

    Wraps components/ui/_empty_state in the tr/td plumbing so callers do not
    repeat the colspan arithmetic. This block was previously copy-pasted into
    five admin index pages, each with slightly different copy and none with a
    call to action - so a new admin was told "create your first X" and left to
    find the button themselves.

    Locals:
      colspan      - number of columns to span
      title        - short heading
      body         - optional explanatory sentence
      icon         - optional Lucide name (default: inbox)

    **No action.** It took `action_label` / `action_path` and rendered a `tw-btn-primary`, which put a
    second filled button for the same destination on four indexes and the classroom roster - the page
    header already carries "New teacher", "New student" and the rest. An empty state explains why a list
    is empty and what will fill it; the page header acts. That way the button is in one place whether the
    list has nothing in it or a hundred rows, instead of moving when the first record lands. %>
<tr>
  <td colspan="<%= colspan %>" class="p-0">
    <%= render layout: "components/ui/empty_state",
               locals: { title: title,
                         body: local_assigns[:body],
                         icon: local_assigns.fetch(:icon, "inbox") } do %><% end %>
  </td>
</tr>
